/* The window, driven for real.
 *
 * The Rust gates read this window's source; they cannot lay it out. Anything
 * whose truth is a measurement — a control's computed width, a label that
 * either does or does not fit inside its dialog — has to be asserted against
 * a browser that actually performed the layout, which is what this is for.
 *
 *   node ui/tests/window.mjs                         the whole gate
 *   WINDOW_SUITES=workers node ui/tests/window.mjs   one suite, by name or pattern
 *   node ui/tests/window.mjs --suite workers         the same, on the command line
 *
 * The suites are registered below in the order the full run takes them; the
 * runner (`window-runner.mjs`) chooses, collects, turns a suite's uncaught
 * exception into one FAIL line and prints the lane's report.
 *
 * Playwright is pinned by the repository. A missing package or browser is a
 * broken test environment, not a passing layout check.
 */


